# NestIQ Design System — Typography Rules

When editing any frontend file, follow these rules exactly.
Do not deviate based on your own design judgment.

## Fonts
- Headlines + body: DM Sans (`var(--font-sans)`)
- All data, prices, scores, counts, tags: DM Mono (`var(--font-mono)`)
- Never use Inter, system-ui, or any other font family

## Type Scale (use only these values)
- 12px → `var(--text-xs)` — captions, timestamps
- 14px → `var(--text-sm)` — secondary body, metadata
- 16px → `var(--text-base)` — primary body copy
- 20px → `var(--text-md)` — card titles, subheadings
- 24px → `var(--text-lg)` — section headers
- 32px → `var(--text-xl)` — page titles
- 40px → `var(--text-2xl)` — hero subheadline
- 52px → `var(--text-3xl)` — hero headline (landing only)

Never hardcode a font-size in px, rem, or em. Always use a token.

## Weights
- 300 → h1, h2, hero display text only
- 400 → body copy, descriptions
- 500 → buttons, nav, labels, tags
- Never use 600, 700, or bold — anywhere

## Tracking (letter-spacing)
- Hero (52px): `var(--tracking-tight)` = -0.03em
- h1/h2 (40/32px): `var(--tracking-snug)` = -0.015em
- Body: `var(--tracking-normal)` = 0em
- Small labels: `var(--tracking-wide)` = 0.06em
- Eyebrow/all-caps: `var(--tracking-wider)` = 0.1em

## Leading (line-height)
- Hero + h1/h2: `var(--leading-tight)` = 1.15
- h3/h4/card titles: `var(--leading-snug)` = 1.3
- Body copy: `var(--leading-normal)` = 1.55
- Pulse prose: `var(--leading-relaxed)` = 1.7

## Utility Classes (apply in JSX)
- `.type-hero` — landing page headline only
- `.type-eyebrow` — small all-caps label above a section
- `.type-secondary` — metadata, muted descriptions
- `.type-prose` — Pulse article body
- `.type-data` — prices, scores, counts (14px DM Mono)
- `.type-data-lg` — primary rent price on cards (20px DM Mono)
- `.type-label` — buttons, nav items, filter tags

## Amber (#E8A020)
- Used on one word or value per section maximum
- Never on entire headlines or paragraphs
- Never as a background on text blocks

## Hard Rules
- No font-weight 600 or 700 anywhere
- No Inter anywhere
- No arbitrary font sizes outside the scale
- No DM Sans on prices, scores, or numeric data
- No all-caps except `.type-eyebrow` at 12px
- No inline style overrides for typography — use tokens and utility classes
